# Reviewed source inputs. Change these in a commit, together with adaptation notes.
#
# Default build combination: XanMod 7.2.9 + EL2 + KernelSU + Clang ThinLTO, with
# SC8280XP tuning (-march=armv8.4-a+crypto -mtune=cortex-x1c). The CI workflows
# default to this combination: kernel_base=xanmod, kernel_tag=KERNEL_XANMOD_TAG,
# build_el2=true, build_kernelsu=true, kernel_toolchain=clang, kernel_tune=sc8280xp.
#
# Source-input exception: this file pins the *mainline* checkout (KERNEL_TAG and
# KERNEL_COMMIT below). XanMod is a separate source selected by KERNEL_BASE=xanmod;
# its tag is KERNEL_XANMOD_TAG, and for an XanMod build the naming label KERNEL_TAG
# must equal that tag. The package workflows enforce the equality and refuse a
# mismatch, and build.sh preserves a caller-provided KERNEL_TAG, so a local XanMod
# build must pass KERNEL_TAG=7.2.9-xanmod1 (see README.md). KERNEL_BASE is
# intentionally left unset here so the local default stays the pinned mainline
# commit; only the CI workflows default to XanMod.
# The kernel commit below is published on the gaokun3 branch.
KERNEL_REPOSITORY=gaokun3/linux
KERNEL_TAG=gaokun3
KERNEL_COMMIT=73033564068250603f5b2150c408554faaf22d66
# EL2 is patch-based: scripts/ci/20_build_kernel_variants.sh applies
# patches/el2 (plus any patches/xanmod/el2 overrides) on top of the prepared
# KERN_SRC tree. There is no separate EL2 commit to check out, so this stays
# empty and is not required for BUILD_EL2=true. It is still exported because the
# Fedora and Ubuntu image workflows read it unconditionally under `set -u`.
KERNEL_EL2_COMMIT=
FEDORA_RELEASE=44
UBUNTU_RELEASE=26.04
